ISO-10303-21;
HEADER;
FILE_DESCRIPTION(('ViewDefinition[DesignTransferView]'),'2;1');
FILE_NAME('bonsai-door-symbols.ifc','2026-11-25T00:00:00',('IfcSheet'),('IfcSheet'),'hand-written in the shape IfcOpenShell 0.8 / Bonsai writes','gen_fixture.py','');
FILE_SCHEMA(('IFC4'));
ENDSEC;
DATA;
/* #831: one storey of 2.7 m walls, Bonsai-style. Exterior walls 0.3 m (footprint (0,0) (6,0) (9,3) (9,7) (0,7), the second wall oblique
   at 45 degrees), layers to the inside, material layer set usage and Pset_WallCommon.IsExternal; a 0.1 m partition at x = 5.
   Each door and window fills a real IfcOpeningElement (IfcRelVoidsElement, IfcRelFillsElement), is placed relative to it, and maps its
   body from its type (IfcRepresentationMap), as Bonsai writes them. D01: 0.9 m entrance door in the south wall at x 2.0 to 2.9, type
   SINGLE_SWING_LEFT, whose type also maps a Plan / Body / PLAN_VIEW Curve2D symbol. D02: 0.8 m door in the partition at y 3.3 to 4.1,
   type SINGLE_SWING_RIGHT. W01: 1.2 m window (DOUBLE_PANEL_VERTICAL) in the oblique wall, 1.5 to 2.7 m along it, sill 0.9 m. W02:
   0.9 m window (SINGLE_PANEL) in the north wall, 3.0 to 3.9 m along it from (9,7). As IfcOpenShell's feature.add_filling leaves them,
   no IfcRelContainedInSpatialStructure contains the doors and windows: they are on the storey only through the wall they fill. */
